@node Glossary
@chapter Glossary

@itemize
@item
@strong{@strong{GNU/Linux}}: A free and open-source operating system combining the GNU system and the Linux kernel.
@item
@strong{@strong{Lisp Machine}}: A type of computer optimized for running Lisp, a family of programming languages.
@item
@strong{@strong{GNU Guix}}: A functional package management tool and standalone distribution of the GNU system.
@item
@strong{@strong{REPL (Read Eval Print Loop)}}: An interactive programming environment for evaluating code and seeing immediate results.
@item
@strong{@strong{TTY (TeleTYpewriter)}}: A text terminal for interacting with a computer system.
@item
@strong{@strong{Scheme}}: A Lisp dialect often used for scripting in GNU Guix.
@item
@strong{@strong{Wayland}}: A protocol for a display server, often used as a modern alternative to X11.
@item
@strong{@strong{Sway}}: A Wayland compositor compatible with i3-style window management.
@item
@strong{@strong{PipeWire}}: A modern multimedia framework for managing audio and video streams.
@item
@strong{@strong{Elpaca}}: A package manager for Emacs that supports advanced configuration options.
@item
@strong{@strong{Libre}}: Free and open-source software that respects user freedom.
@end itemize

